# Tern: Engine

- `game/portrait.js` is pure logic that also runs in node; keep scoring there and keep it testable.
- `game/index.html` holds the map and UI. Worlds past the park are `REGIONS` (bounds, optional `walk` rectangle and `fogArea`), each with its own random sequence for scenery. Never change an earlier world's street control points or random sequence; filter afterwards so its layout never shifts.
- Every building has a footprint (`FOOT` or the houses/towers lists); the player routes around them (`walkTo`). Stands sit outside footprints.
- A new world needs: `content-<world>.js`, `scenes-<world>.js`, an entry in `content.worlds` (chapter, closeTo, ladder), a region, `PLACES` + `FOOT`, a `LOOKS` framing, and streets joined to the previous world's at exactly the same end points.
- Test with node checks and a headless Chrome over DevTools (cache disabled; test on `127.0.0.1:8123` to keep a separate save). The browser pane pauses animation while hidden.
